munication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Candidate D has responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but arrogance, weak leadership, hot temper (though not in original). Candidate A has anticipation, spatial vision, leadership, but unorganized, poor at criticism, not open to new ideas.\n\nWhich candidate best balances? For long-distance flights, reliability, calmness, decision-making, teamwork are crucial. B's teamwork issues could be problematic for crew. C's communication difficulty and egocentric attitude could also be problematic, but they create positive atmosphere? Contradiction. C is 100% reliable, calm, quick decisions, positive atmosphere, but difficulty communicating ideas (maybe can be mitigated). Also not willing to further education, but long-term suitability may be less critical if already competent.\n\nD's arrogance and weak leadership may affect crew. A's unorganized and not open to new ideas may affect long flights.\n\nThus candidate C seems strong on reliability, calmness, decision-making, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be mitigated. B's teamwork issues are more severe (uncooperative, nasty remarks). So I might shift to Candidate C as provisional preference.\n\nWe need to state our current preferred candidate, summarizing evidence, including Agent 2's provisional preference and answer. Also note uncertainties: C's communication difficulty and lack of willingness to further education; B's teamwork issues; D's arrogance; A's unorganized.\n\nWhat would change vote: Positive info on B's teamwork, or negative info on C's communication, etc.\n\nNow produce public message."}
